// The Shell dialog's preview on a 30 mm cube with every edge rounded 5 (the "extrude test"
// document), its top's flat and four rounds removed, 2 mm: the result opaque as it will be, the
// material the shell takes out (inward) or adds (outward) faint over it, the removed faces
// yellow over everything, and the thickness arrow on the first of them.
// 01 inward.
// 02 the arrow dragged along itself: thicker walls, live.
// 03 outward (the walls round over the cube's rounds as Onshape's do; the removed rounds' slabs
//    go straight through).
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        Custom("fixture rounded_cube_shell"),
        Key("P"),
        Key("F"),
        DoubleClick(ui("feature-shell-1")),
        WaitFor("shell-dialog"),
        WaitFor("shell-thickness-arrow"),
        MoveTo(1420, 900),
        Wait(5),
        Screenshot("01-inward-preview"),
        Drag(ui("shell-thickness-arrow"), ui_at("shell-thickness-arrow", 0.5, 2.5)),
        MoveTo(1420, 900),
        Wait(5),
        Screenshot("02-arrow-dragged"),
        Click(ui("shell-thickness-flip")),
        MoveTo(1420, 900),
        Wait(5),
        Screenshot("03-outward-preview"),
    ],
)
